@startuml "Pytition Settings Structure"
title Pytition Settings Structure — config.settings

!include modern-dark.puml

node "config.settings\n(__init__.py)" as ENTRY
component DJANGO as "django.py\n(core Django settings)"
component DEFAULT as "default.py\n(app/project defaults)"
package "delta/" {
  component DEV as "dev.py\n(env delta)"
  component PROD as "prod.py\n(env delta)"
  component TEST as "test.py\n(env delta)"
}

database DOTENV as ".env (file)"
database OSENV as "OS Environment Variables"
component DETECT as "Environment detection\n(_detect_env: ENV/DEBUG)"
component OVERRIDE as "override_settings_from_env()"
collections GLOB as "globals() (effective settings)"

' Base imports
ENTRY --> DJANGO : import *
ENTRY --> DEFAULT : import *

' Environment detection
ENTRY --> DETECT : resolve active ENV
DETECT --> DEV  : if ENV=dev
DETECT --> PROD : if ENV=prod
DETECT --> TEST : if ENV=test

' Import delta based on ENV
ENTRY --> DEV  : import * (when dev)
ENTRY --> PROD : import * (when prod)
ENTRY --> TEST : import * (when test)

' Detection sources
DOTENV --> DETECT : ENV / DEBUG (highest precedence)
OSENV  --> DETECT : fallback

' Final overrides
DJANGO  --> OVERRIDE
DEFAULT --> OVERRIDE
DEV     --> OVERRIDE
PROD    --> OVERRIDE
TEST    --> OVERRIDE

DOTENV --> OVERRIDE : UPPERCASE keys\n(priority 1)
OSENV  --> OVERRIDE : UPPERCASE keys\n(priority 2)
OVERRIDE --> GLOB   : apply updates

note right of OVERRIDE
Value precedence:
  1) .env
  2) OS env vars
  3) Python defaults (django.py, default.py, delta/*.py)

Type casting:
  • bool: "1/true/yes/on"
  • ast.literal_eval for int/float/dict/list/tuple
  • lists: comma-split fallback when needed
end note
@enduml
